A||||5||Formula 18||Why do 88 have smaller Front rims? ||||5||
Z||000000||Formula 18||03-05-2001||01:43 AM||||I was looking at new rims and thought about the fact that the fronts are an inch smaller that the backs? Why is this just on 88's (new suspension desgin)? <P>What would happen if you went to say 15x6.5 15x7 all around? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||03-05-2001||07:27 AM||||The wheel offsets were different for the 88s because, as you realized, of the 88 suspension redesign.  I don't know enough about the potential for different wheels and how they would fit. Do a search on previous posts as there is a lot of "information" in the forum on the use of different size wheels.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Will||03-05-2001||10:36 AM||||I ran '87 15 x 7 wheels on '88 front suspension with no ill effects. It was a nice setup. The extra width on the inner edge of the wheel reduces the scrub radius and makes the steering even lighter.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||03-05-2001||11:55 AM||||The front wheels on the 88's are different because the steering rack is 1" wider than previous years. By running earlier year wheels, your wheels and tires will stick out of the fenderwell more.  I don't know if that'll hurt anything, but I think it looks silly.  Makes the car look like it's wearing clown shoes, IMHO. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||ThatRickGuy||03-05-2001||12:00 PM||||I ran into a problem w/ this when I had some work done on the car, the mechanic put the wheels on incorrectly, 1 rear tire was up front. This made stearing at low speeds extremely difficult and also chewed up the inner edge of the tire. I'd argue for some money, but the tires are old as heck anyways.||||reg||1
Z||000005||My7Fieros||03-05-2001||01:37 PM||||Ive got 15x7's all the way around on my Formula...I think it looks great (looks like a bulldog up front lol)..also, the thing steers like its got power steering! I love it. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-009f_6.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://tgowens.com/My7Fieros_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
